 "response": "Gikistu's budget is now **$3098K**.\n\n**How I worked it out**\n\n1. **Which records count.** Only Finance Office budget updates change the budget. Every PMO, Engineering, Sales, Vendor, Legal, Marketing, Operations and Facilities message is ignored. So are Finance Office items that don't touch the budget, such as room moves, archived invoices and reminders.\n2. **Withdrawal chains.** I traced each chain back from its last link. A withdrawal counts only if it has not itself been effectively withdrawn. For example:\n   - #0003 stays withdrawn. The chain runs #0694 \u2192 #0535 \u2192 #0435 \u2192 #0357 \u2192 #0206 \u2192 #0202 \u2192 #0145 \u2192 #0011 \u2192 #0005 \u2192 #0003, so the withdrawals alternate and #0005 ends up in force.\n   - #0002 stays in effect. #0843 cancels #0754, which restores #0019, which cancels #0008.\n   - The other reinstated updates work the same way. Examples are #0013, #0036, #0066, #0077, #0079, #0126, #0312, #0365, #0368, #0655, #0852 and #0980.\n3. **Applying the updates.** I started from the $2070K set in #0001. I then applied every remaining Finance Office increase and decrease once, in record order, skipping all withdrawn updates. The running total ends at $3098K.\n\nI did not do a separate second pass to recheck the arithmetic.\n\nANSWER: $3098K",
